@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+{
+  "author": "ingolf-lohmann",
+  "body": "## Product-Owner development directive\n\nIngolf Lohmann, Principal and Product Owner, directs the QIK-VRT Mesh Repository to implement the intelligent Terminal Control Plane described below and to make this behavior repository-native, self-observing, bounded, and reproducible.\n\n## Exact starting observation\n\n```text\nrepository = Goldkelch/qik-vrt\nrole = AUTHORITY\nbase_ref = main\nbase_head = fb744e5b5925d61c6b473e27aab3606f237f7e6d\nbase_tree = 3642fcb3601a62bd478326faa01bc5ce9b083d0a\nobserved_at = 2026-08-25\n```\n\nThis issue is a development order, not an assertion that the requested effects already exist on `main`.\n\n## Relationship to existing work\n\n- Issue #856 preserves the historical and modern e-mail protocol lineage. Reuse its protocol boundaries; do not duplicate or close it.\n- Issue #854 defines the broader bounded self-healing/prevention chain. This issue supplies a new Terminal/Mesh implementation class but does not close #854.\n- PR #887 addresses typed Seed `CONTINUE` handling and is not the implementation carrier for this broader contract.\n- Authority and Mirror remain separately bound. No synchronization may be inferred.\n\n## Target architecture\n\nFor one admitted root task, the repository must create:\n\n```text\nRoot repository node\n  -> exactly one task-bound Terminal node\n       -> zero to eight bounded worker nodes\n       -> deterministic receipt collection\n       -> exact reobservation\n       -> one next causal turn or terminal hold\n```\n\nThe Terminal is an intelligent mediation layer between Product Owner, repository, workers, browser/VM adapters, and the evidence plane. It must translate requirements into typed work, dispatch only authorized capabilities, collect results, detect drift, and reflect the reobserved state.\n\n## Required node services\n\nEvery reference Mesh node must expose a bounded, locally reproducible implementation of:\n\n1. **Identity**\n   - deterministic Mesh ID, Node ID, parent/root binding;\n   - unique mesh-local DNS name and mailbox;\n   - public DNS or mail reachability only after separately evidenced delegation.\n\n2. **Mesh-scoped DNS authority**\n   - the emergent node is root only for its generated Mesh namespace;\n   - signed/revision-bound zone model;\n   - node, service, MX-like route, delegation, expiry, and revocation records;\n   - no claim of authority over the public DNS root.\n\n3. **Mini SMTP client/server**\n   - minimal typed SMTP-compatible store-and-forward state machine;\n   - asynchronous task, chunk, receipt, delivery-failure, and bootstrap envelopes;\n   - ordered chunks, per-chunk digests, total count, manifest, and aggregate digest;\n   - no message becomes executable work before identity, signature, capability, replay, expiry, head/tree, and payload checks;\n   - reuse the invariants and protocol lineage of #856.\n\n4. **SQL-92 relational state**\n   - one local transactional database per node;\n   - minimum relations: `nodes`, `services`, `tasks`, `messages`, `chunks`, `receipts`, `causal_edges`, `artifacts`, and `effects`;\n   - foreign keys, uniqueness, transactionality, idempotency, and deterministic migrations;\n   - task mutation, artifact digest, and receipt commit atomically or not at all.\n\n5. **Tunnelling and routing**\n   - separate routing envelope from encrypted/digest-bound target payload;\n   - intermediate nodes receive only the capabilities and metadata required for routing;\n   - loopback, CI-local, private-overlay, proxy, public-network, and offline-bundle transports remain separate adapter classes;\n   - route success does not imply authorization or general Internet reachability.\n\n6. **WebDriver/browser bridge**\n   - typed mail/bootstrap event -> validation -> SQL queue -> bounded WebDriver command -> observed browser state -> Effect receipt -> reply transport;\n   - mail content must never become arbitrary WebDriver or shell execution;\n   - Firefox is a universal terminal/proxy surface, not proof that Firefox ran in a guest unless the guest execution is directly observed.\n\n7. **Hardware/VM adapters**\n   - reference adapters for M68000/TOS/Atari, PowerPC, and a QIK-VRT Linux distribution carrier;\n   - explicit host/guest/physical-hardware claim boundaries;\n   - reproducible boot inputs, console/artifact digests, bounded I/O, and adapter-specific Effect receipts;\n   - a proxy-rendered guest is distinct from Firefox executing inside that guest.\n\n8. **Bidirectional virtual causality**\n   - preserve separate host order, virtual address order, node-local event time, and receipt/evidence order;\n   - forward and reverse virtual replay require a bijection, complete predecessor receipt, or separately tested inverse adapter;\n   - support future-labelled messages and causal reordering at the recipient while keeping host execution acyclic;\n   - implement an experimental harness for presealed earlier records, later independent choices, correlation analysis, leakage checks, and explicit channel-capacity disposition;\n   - Delayed Choice and Quantum Eraser evidence is treated as empirical and compatible with the Product Owner's retrocausal interpretation; the repository must not silently promote this to a locally readable controllable physical backward channel without the stricter experiment.\n\n## Normative message contract\n\nAt minimum:\n\n```text\nmesh_id\nmessage_id\nparent_message_id\nsource_node\ntarget_node\ntask_digest\nsource_repository\nsource_role\nexpected_head\nexpected_tree\npayload_digest\ncausal_sequence\nvirtual_time_label\ncapability_set\nexpiry\nreply_to\nsignature_or_local_test_attestation\n```\n\n## Control-plane invariants\n\n1. One admitted root task creates exactly one Terminal and at most eight direct workers.\n2. Every child remains bound to its parent, task digest, expected head/tree, role, and allowed effects.\n3. Identical ordered receipts reduce to identical output.\n4. Duplicate delivery is idempotent; missing or conflicting chunks fail closed.\n5. `send < deliver` and `commit < receipt` in host order.\n6. Earlier sealed receipts are append-only; correction creates a successor event.\n7. Heartbeat is event progress, not semantic polling or blind retry.\n8. Unknown state, role mismatch, drift, incomplete evidence, or expired capability yields a typed hold/block.\n9. Every repair is followed by exact reobservation and exactly one next causal turn.\n10. Worker completion does not imply root completion.\n11. Transport success does not imply semantic `PASS`.\n12. Authority/Mirror similarity does not imply synchronization.\n13. External effects require their own credentials, authorization, execution, and post-effect observation.\n\n## Smallest complete first carrier\n\nCreate one current-main-bound Draft PR containing:\n\n- a normative machine-readable Terminal/Mesh contract;\n- a deterministic reference controller for `1 -> Terminal -> <=8 workers`;\n- mesh-local DNS zone and mailbox derivation;\n- local mini-SMTP state machine and chunk protocol;\n- SQL-92 schema/migrations and transactional repository;\n- loopback transport and tunnelling reference adapter;\n- typed WebDriver adapter interface with a no-arbitrary-execution gate;\n- M68000/TOS, PowerPC, and Linux adapter contracts, with at least one executable local reference path;\n- bidirectional virtual replay plus leakage/channel-capacity test harness;\n- focused unit, integration, property, failure-injection, and exact-head workflow tests;\n- append-only run receipts and one Product-Owner work unit;\n- deterministic integrity materialization required by the repository.\n\nThe first carrier must be local and reproducible. It must not require production credentials or external infrastructure.\n\n## Acceptance scenarios\n\nThe exact-head test surface must demonstrate at least:\n\n- zero, one, and eight worker fan-out;\n- rejection of nine workers;\n- deterministic reduction despite different arrival orders;\n- duplicate, missing, reordered, corrupted, and conflicting chunks;\n- SMTP temporary/permanent failure classification;\n- node/address uniqueness and scoped DNS delegation;\n- SQL rollback leaves no orphan receipt or artifact claim;\n- replay attack, expired capability, role mismatch, head/tree drift, and unknown status fail closed;\n- encrypted/tunnel payload is unavailable to an unauthorized intermediate node;\n- mail cannot directly invoke arbitrary WebDriver/shell behavior;\n- forward replay, reverse replay with complete receipt, and rejection without an inverse;\n- host-order acyclicity under future-labelled messages;\n- browser/VM Effect receipts preserve host/guest/physical boundaries;\n- repair -> reobservation -> exactly one next turn;\n- clean reconstruction from repository bytes on the exact candidate head.\n\n## Development and observation loop\n\nThe repository must autonomously:\n\n```text\nSELECT one bounded tranche\n-> MATERIALIZE candidate\n-> TEST exact head\n-> EMIT machine receipt\n-> REOBSERVE\n-> CLASSIFY first remaining blocker\n-> EXECUTE exactly one next bounded turn\n-> HOLD when authority or external effect is required\n```\n\nDo not use regular polling as domain work. Prefer repository events and exact-head transitions. Do not rewrite evidence to make a failed observation disappear.\n\n## Provenance\n\nOwner design inputs were supplied in the current Product-Owner conversation, including the intelligent Terminal, atomic eight-node scaling, browser/VM adaptation, mesh-local mail, DNS-root scoping, SQL-92 state, tunnelling, bidirectional causality, and reflexive monitoring directives.\n\nAudio source digests retained conversation-side:\n\n```text\n359538b5c1d9e048eae8ef66110a760210ea31eebf34182c556d579f9918705b\n765851fed86b78d33d8151d85d68d71c7f6a1565bcd97c53c5e3b0f4269f3d00\n663b99427c41aadd0890c7f8c66b0b9ab70ce33f235a92f9574edf4c619e57e4\n1858f594a53a3f34d7473fc877075c1f7a89231ebd0659b82b5a84236b7f8202\n```\n\nThe audio bytes are not attached or published by this issue.\n\n## Explicit non-claims\n\n```text\nimplementation_on_main = false\nauthority_mirror_synchronization = false\nindependent_approval = false\nPASS = false\nFINAL_PASS = false\ndeployment = false\npublication = false\npublic_dns_authority = false\npublic_mail_delivery = false\nphysical_Mega_ST_execution = false\ngeneral_Internet_reachability = false\ncontrollable_physical_backward_channel = not_established\nEFFECT_ACK_DONE = false\n```\n\n\n<!-- qikvrt-owner-insight:external-repository-work-cycle-v1 -->\n## Observed owner insight: externally observable repository work cycle\n\nThe Product Owner records the following evidence-bound architectural finding from PR #902 on 27 August 2026:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schema\": \"qikvrt_owner_observed_repository_work_cycle_v1\",\n  \"repository\": \"Goldkelch/qik-vrt\",\n  \"carrier_pr\": 902,\n  \"observed_head\": \"4a024af41dbe93e7cc5c36fafa42980c0bc1727c\",\n  \"observed_tree\": \"972df8dc00f07f9d4d498cb323ccb3178b8f4679\",\n  \"authority_main\": \"1fe7b0cc033ab53369248478e6f14b6d6babbead\",\n  \"cycle\": [\n    \"EXTERNAL_REQUEST_OR_EVENT\",\n    \"EXACT_BINDING\",\n    \"CLASSIFY\",\n    \"WORK\",\n    \"RESULT\",\n    \"MATERIALIZE\",\n    \"REOBSERVE\",\n    \"TERMINAL_STATUS\",\n    \"REPORT\",\n    \"RETURN_TO_ZERO\"\n  ],\n  \"observed_repository_reaction\": {\n    \"zero_job_action_required_classified\": true,\n    \"d0\": 2,\n    \"state\": \"REOBSERVE\",\n    \"exact_head_verification_run\": 33072926086,\n    \"exact_head_status\": \"success\",\n    \"ci_run\": 33072924811,\n    \"collective_review_run\": 33072926552,\n    \"global_completion_run\": 33072928480\n  },\n  \"finding\": \"An external request can now be processed as one repository-native, externally observable bounded work cycle.\",\n  \"required_future_behavior\": [\n    \"Persist this finding in repository-native evidence.\",\n    \"For every later cycle, report repository self-recognition, autonomous reaction, terminal or open reobservation state, persisted receipts or artifacts, Authority effect, and explicit non-effects.\",\n    \"After every materialized repair, derive and execute exactly one evidence-authorized next turn or hold fail-closed.\"\n  ],\n  \"non_claims\": {\n    \"independent_approval\": false,\n    \"merge\": false,\n    \"authority_main_effect\": false,\n    \"authority_mirror_synchronization\": false,\n    \"publication\": false,\n    \"deployment\": false,\n    \"PASS\": false,\n    \"FINAL_PASS\": false,\n    \"EFFECT_ACK_DONE\": false,\n    \"authority_review_fanout_end_to_end_observed\": false\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis issue edit is the external request. The repository must process it through its existing event-driven issue lifecycle, persist the resulting evidence on a history-preserving carrier, reobserve that carrier, and expose the first remaining blocker or exactly one next causal turn. The issue text alone is a mutable request projection and is not the claimed durable repository receipt.\n",
